Third-party material
====================

src/gavel_harness/rubric/library_v1/
  Rubric library: 19,603 entries in six domains, built without any model call by
  src/gavel_harness/rubric/build.py from the two sources below. Every entry
  keeps its source text verbatim (whitespace runs collapsed to one space) and
  names the source task it came from.

  1. Domains finance, legal, finance_hard, legal_hard (18,828 entries)
     Source:  PRBench: Large-Scale Expert Rubrics for Evaluating High-Stakes
              Professional Reasoning, by Scale AI.
              https://huggingface.co/datasets/ScaleAI/PRBench
              Splits finance, legal, finance_hard, legal_hard; the parquet files
              used have sha256
                finance       4e3d790d00eefdc9ec7090a2e19459e74c1788921c525b3d14ed0dbf1f155dc0
                legal         3d80ca175eaf5072880f33fd28e74a610ab99cc74e6c5b173d89312365a7c67f
                finance_hard  5218eeb81834b8d0786b0b1ee414dbf7f563fcd01f355420d48376614af04b2a
                legal_hard    9eebf855786e9b7c719ae80ad58fab0aba184b5406944e8c5b9d9cebcdb32895
     License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
              https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
     Changes: only the task, topic and rubric fields were read. For finance and
              legal, only tasks that a deterministic hash split (salt
              "rubric-v1") assigns to the library half were used; the other half
              is held out for evaluation. finance_hard and legal_hard were used
              in full. Each rubric criterion became one entry holding its title,
              description and category verbatim; its weight class was mapped to
              one of three severity levels (critically important / important,
              slightly important, detrimental classes); criteria with any other
              weight class were left out. Entries were numbered and grouped into
              one Markdown file per category, with a per-domain README.md and
              INDEX.tsv written for this library.

